// Tessera stdlib: the correctly rounded natural logarithm of F64
//
// x = 2^e y with y in [1/sqrt(2), sqrt(2)), and r_i y - 1 = z exactly for a
// 10-bit reciprocal r_i from a table: log x = e log(2) - log(r_i) + log(1 + z),
// with a degree-6 polynomial, as a double-double. When that can't decide the
// rounding (about once in 2^11.5), the accurate path redoes it in "dint"
// arithmetic: 128-bit significands with an exponent and a sign, a second
// table reduction and a degree-13 polynomial. Round to nearest only:
// log(+-0) is -inf, a negative input gives NaN, NaN comes back quiet, and
// log(1) = +0.
//
// The dint helpers and the accurate path (cm_f64_log_dint_*) are shared with
// log10 (Log10.tess). The fast path's double-double also gives F64.log(self,
// base) its first tier (cm_f64_log_dd, cm_f64_log_ratio_fast).
//
// Ported from CORE-MATH, src/binary64/log/log.c and its dint.h via
// RazorForge's B64Log.rf.
// log.c: Copyright (c) 2022 INRIA and CERN. Authors: Paul Zimmermann and Tom Hubrecht.
// dint.h: Copyright (c) 2022 CERN. Author: Tom Hubrecht.
// MIT license: see LICENSE-CORE-MATH

module Standard::Core

/// Reciprocals r[i] of the fast path, 362 <= i <= 724, as F64 bits: a 10-bit approximation of 1/y for
/// i 2^-9 <= y < (i + 1) 2^-9 such that r[i] y - 1 is exact (the entries for i = 511, 512 are forced to 1).
